{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>עד</b>: The sense is 'I will not be moved'—on the plan of a man that he would be moved; therefore he rebukes them, saying עד אנה תהותתו. From the root רי\"ש תרצחו, kamatz gadol, therefore it is a verb whose noun is not called [by a nominal form], like ובמים לא רוחצת, for the kamatz and the shureq and the cholam are found in this binyan, and this is the way of prayer." "<b>And the sense of כקיר נטוי</b>—that you are thus, and נטוי is on the pattern of עצום, or it is of the verbs that are transitive [יוצאים] and [the matter] is pushed off [to a different construction], and the sense is doubled."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 62, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:32.086619242Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}